cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this tool or its method in a paper, a report or a comparison, please cite it as below."
title: "tennis-api-benchmark: measure any tennis API against a published method"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-23"
authors:
  - name: "Live Tennis API"
    website: "https://livetennisapi.com"
    email: "hello@livetennisapi.com"
repository-code: "https://gitlab.com/livetennisapi/tennis-api-benchmark"
url: "https://gitlab.com/livetennisapi/tennis-api-benchmark"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A small Python tool that measures the response time and observed
  availability of a tennis data API from one stated vantage point. It
  refuses to print a percentile from too few clean samples and never counts
  a rate-limit response as downtime. The arithmetic lives in one module with
  no network code, so anyone can check it. It is published by JSB Holdings
  LLC, which operates Live Tennis API, and works against any provider.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - API testing
  - latency
  - availability
  - reproducibility
  - sports data
  - tennis
